From fa4c5bf57a84112afbaf822d7fb6c158e5e52c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinko Korunic <dinko.korunic@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:18:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] SubGHz: add Proteco MOVER protocol

Proteco MOVER gate remotes (433.92 MHz AM650, 24 bit fixed code) use CAME
line coding at Te ~440us instead of 320us, so the CAME decoder rejected them
and they only worked as RAW. Adds decoder and encoder, unit tests and docs.
https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperzero-firmware/issues/2345
---
SubGHz: add Proteco MOVER protocol (433.92 MHz AM650, 24 bit static)

Proteco MOVER gate remotes (Italy) use CAME line coding at Te ~440us
instead of 320us, so the CAME decoder rejects every long pulse and the
remote only worked as RAW. Adds decode, save and send, custom buttons
(the low 2 bits of the key: A, B, C on a Proteco TX3, plus a fourth code),
an Add Manually entry ("Proteco 433MHz"), and unit tests for buttons
A, B and C. https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperzero-firmware/issues/2345

Merged into Unleashed dev as 57d471868 (PR #1210, 2026-11-09): trees
from then on already have it. This file is the three commits of that PR,
for trees that don't:
  1/3 SubGHz: add Proteco MOVER protocol
  2/3 SubGHz: Proteco Add Manually entry, B/C button decoder tests
  3/3 proteco custom buttons, guard checked against frame te (by xMasterX,
      Unleashed maintainer: custom buttons, guard checked against the
      frame's own Te, CHANGELOG entry)

Apply from the root of an Unleashed firmware checkout, either
    git am proteco-mover-subghz.patch          (keeps the three commits)
or  git apply --3way proteco-mover-subghz.patch   (one uncommitted change)
or  patch -p1 < proteco-mover-subghz.patch

Made against Unleashed dev 1fe237846 (2026-11). Needs a tree that has the
shared helpers in lib/subghz/protocols/common.h (dev from 2026-08-31 / PR
#1116 on). The hunks likely to drift:
- CHANGELOG.md (3/3): its top changes every release. If it does not
  apply, leave it out: add --exclude=CHANGELOG.md to git am / git apply.
- protocol_items.c/.h: if --3way leaves a conflict, keep upstream's lines
  and append `&subghz_protocol_proteco,` / `#include "proteco.h"` as the
  last entries. Keep them at the end: higher up in the list, clang-format
  (./fbt lint) wants the whole registry reflowed.
- subghz_custom_event.h / subghz_scene_set_type.c (Add Manually): both
  lists are sorted by menu name; put `SetTypeProteco433` right after the
  Princeton 433MHz entry.

